- op: discuss  # 00a2
  at: '2026-08-01T05:34:34Z'  # 00a2
  by: agent  # 00a2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 00a2
  clock: 13  # 00a2
  nonce: 00a2  # 00a2
  message: "BAKEOFF VALIDATION: INCONCLUSIVE — tag KEPT. Two datasets, neither decisive:\n  1. Reflect assessments (deep-20260717-200119): no_move=7 / moved=1 — but\n     measured on the hg.4k/16k/64k budget views, the instrument the\n     2026-07-16 correction on WI-kolal established as the wrong path for\n     compact-subcommand claims. Not actionable alone.\n  2. Right-instrument probe (dev 54a5f34bcc, compact --max-symbols 10,\n     default = centrality-ranked per the fix): overlap between the selected\n     10 and the input map's top-10 by the stored node `centrality` field is\n     only 20-50% across the eight 07-17 maps (caddy 50%, express 30%,\n     apollo 20%, SwiftyJSON 40%, zoxide 40%, petclinic 30%, sherpa 30%,\n     pretix 40%). CAVEAT preventing a no_move verdict: compact's ranking\n     key may legitimately differ from the stored per-node centrality field\n     (kind filtering, internal recomputation, coverage mechanics) — the\n     probe measures key disagreement, not necessarily defect. Deciding\n     needs the item's intended key stated and checked, and the ordering\n     face is still blocked on WI-batit.\nThe aggregate's auto-plan would have spawned a regression item from dataset\n1 alone; withheld. Next validation step: state compact's intended ranking\nkey, then re-run the 10-symbol probe against THAT key."  # 00a2
- op: discuss  # 0b8a
  at: '2026-08-01T20:40:28Z'  # 0b8a
  by: agent  # 0b8a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0b8a
  clock: 14  # 0b8a
  nonce: 0b8a  # 0b8a
  message: "BAKEOFF VALIDATION: INCONCLUSIVE -- tag KEPT. Neither pre-committed threshold fired. But the\nPRIOR measurement on this item is now VOID, which is the substantive result of this round.\n\nTHE 2026-08-01 20-50% OVERLAP FIGURE MEASURED NOTHING. It ranked the input maps by the stored\nper-node \"centrality\" field. That field is present on ZERO nodes across all eight 07-17 maps --\nverified directly by me on the artifacts, not taken from a report: apollo-server 5142 nodes / 0\nwith non-null centrality, caddy 6539/0, express 3833/0, pretix 36603/0, sherpa-csharp 242/0,\nspring-petclinic 1042/0, SwiftyJSON 407/0, zoxide 494/0. Any overlap computed against an absent\nfield is an artifact of the tie-break, not a measurement of ranking disagreement. The caveat the\nprior round recorded (\"the probe measures key disagreement, not necessarily defect\") was\ncorrect to withhold the verdict, but understated: there was no key to disagree with.\n\nCOMPACT'S ACTUAL RANKING KEY, established from source (the step the prior round asked for):\n  - compact.py:933-936 compute_dampened_centrality(symbols, edges, first_party_priority=True) --\n    recomputed internally on every run, never read from a stored node field.\n  - compact.py:969-972 sorted by (-centrality, name).\n  - compact.py:1247 seed_quota = max(1, config.max_symbols // 2); the seed set is force-included\n    ahead of the ranked fill.\n  - The default path select_by_coverage (compact.py:890-1357) applies NO kind filtering.\n\nRE-PROBE UNDER THE CORRECTED KEY, K=10, eight maps (measured by the probe and independently\nre-measured by a second agent instrumenting the real CLI entry point; both got the identical\ntable, which I did not re-run a third time): apollo 5/10, caddy 5/10, express 5/10, pretix 5/10,\nsherpa 5/10, spring-petclinic 6/10, SwiftyJSON 8/10, zoxide 5/10. Against the pre-committed\ncriteria -- moved needs >=80% on >=5 of 8, got 1/8; no_move needs <50% on >=5 of 8, got 0/8.\nNeither fired. INCONCLUSIVE by the criteria as written, so the tag stays.\n\nTWO CORRECTIONS TO CARRY FORWARD, both of which reverse claims made inside this round:\n  1. \"The criteria are unsatisfiable because the seed quota caps overlap near 50%\" is FALSE. The\n     quota is a FLOOR, not a ceiling: overlap = (K - seed_quota) + |seeds intersect ranked-top-K|,\n     so seeds landing in the ranked top-K add to it. SwiftyJSON measured 80% at K=10 in every\n     independent run, which is the bar itself. Do not amend the criteria on unreachability\n     grounds.\n  2. Do NOT replace the criterion with \"the non-seed fill is an exact prefix of the ranked order\"\n     (measured 8/8). Reading compact.py:1012-1020, that walks the sorted list in rank order,\n     skips seeded ids and breaks at the budget -- so it is a prefix of the ranked order for EVERY\n     possible input. It cannot return False. It confirms the CLI reaches select_by_coverage with\n     connectivity_aware=False and nothing downstream reorders, which is worth knowing, but it\n     carries zero discriminating information about the claim.\n  3. The K=100 table from this round is UNUSABLE: it was run with --min-symbols 10 while the K=10\n     table used --min-symbols K, so the coverage stop truncated four selections below budget.\n     Re-measure with a consistent protocol before citing any K=100 number.\n\nTWO FACES MEASURED THAT ARE SCOPE QUESTIONS, NOT VERDICT EVIDENCE under the criteria as written\n-- recorded because they bear on what this item should be scored against, and flagged rather than\nacted on:\n  - Surface agreement, which is this item's own Expectation clause (\"so both surfaces agree\") and\n    its literal title: compact default selected-10 vs production sketch top-10 measured 32.5%\n    (26/80), and 56.2% even after unifying both on compact's key. The root cause measured is\n    population divergence, not the ranking function -- sketch restricts to KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS, drops\n    test paths and tier-4, and uses test-source-free production_edges, while compact's default\n    filters none of it.\n  - Emitted node ORDER against docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:1386 (the line this item quotes verbatim\n    as the violated contract): 0 of 8 maps emit nodes in descending-centrality order, because the\n    force-included seeds occupy the leading positions contiguously. A prior entry (2026-07-16)\n    routed this face wholly to WI-batit as orthogonal; one verifier argues the item's own quoted\n    spec line makes it in-scope here and that the correct verdict is therefore no_move. That is a\n    scope call, not a measurement dispute -- both agents measured the same numbers.\n\nNEW DEFECT FOUND, verified by me in source and filed as its own untagged item: compact's three\nentry points disagree on whether the canonical is_excluded_kind predicate applies.\nselect_by_tokens (compact.py:1421) and format_tiered_behavior_map (compact.py:1720) call it; the\nDEFAULT path select_by_coverage (compact.py:890-1357) never does. The probe measured 17 of 80\nemitted nodes at K=10 as kinds the predicate rejects (file, variable, package), which is likely a\npartial root cause of the WI-batit ordering face, since the leading noise nodes are precisely\nEXCLUDED_KINDS members.\n\nWHAT WOULD DECIDE THIS ITEM NEXT TIME: rule on whether \"centrality-ranked\" binds compact's\nSELECTED SET, its RANKED FILL, or its EMITTED ORDER. The three were measured this round at\n1/8-above-80%, 8/8-but-untestable, and 0/8 respectively -- so the ruling, not another cohort,\nis what converts this item to a verdict."  # 0b8a
