- op: discuss  # 6bc3
  at: '2026-08-01T21:14:25Z'  # 6bc3
  by: agent  # 6bc3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6bc3
  clock: 16  # 6bc3
  nonce: 6bc3  # 6bc3
  message: "OWNER RULING (2026-08-01, walkthrough interview): compact's default should filter the way sketch\ndoes -- reusing sketch's filter function(s) directly where that makes sense.\n\nSTATUS RE-OPENED to todo_hard, tag KEPT. Rationale: this item's title claim (\"sketch and compact\ndisagree on top symbols\") is still TRUE at 32% agreement, and its Expectation clause names\nsurface agreement as the acceptance condition. The 2026-07-09 centrality-default flip landed and\nwas necessary, but it is now measured as insufficient -- closing on it while the title statement\nstill reproduces would be a false close. The tag stays because, unlike WI-lubap, this claim IS\ncohort-testable: sketch-vs-compact top-N agreement is measurable on any repo.\n\nWHY THE RANKING FUNCTION IS NO LONGER THE DISAGREEMENT. Both surfaces now rank with\ncompute_dampened_centrality. Measured on the eight 07-17 maps: sketch top-10 vs compact\ndefault top-10 agree 32% (26/80), and only 56% (45/80) even when both are forced onto an\nidentical ranking key. The residual is POPULATION, not order.\n\nTHE POPULATION DIVERGENCE, located. sketch.py:5742-5748 filters to four clauses:\n    s.kind in KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS          (an allowlist, sketch.py:5712)\n    not _is_test_path(s.path)\n    \"test_\" not in s.name\n    s.supply_chain_tier != 4\nand sketch.py:5754-5757 additionally drops edges originating in test files before computing\ncentrality (production_edges), with exclude_dampeners=(\"file_kind\",) at :5769.\ncompact's default path (select_by_coverage, compact.py:890-1357) applies NONE of this, and does\nnot even apply the project's own is_excluded_kind predicate -- see WI-fadab.\n\nTHE FIX IS AN EXTRACTION, NOT A CALL. There is no reusable sketch filter to import:\nKEY_SYMBOL_KINDS is a frozenset declared INSIDE a function body at sketch.py:5712, and the four\nclauses are an inline comprehension beneath it. Nothing outside that function can reach any of\nit. So the ruling resolves to the chokepoint shape this project's through-line already\nprescribes: give \"what counts as a key symbol\" ONE home, then have sketch and compact's default\nboth consume it. The absence of that home is why the two surfaces could drift at all.\n\nJUDGMENT CALL DEFERRED TO IMPLEMENTATION (flagged, not pre-decided): sketch's kind filter is an\nALLOWLIST of 41 kinds while compact currently filters nothing, so adopting all four clauses\nwholesale would remove kind=\"file\" nodes from compact entirely. D15 makes file-kind nodes the\nper-file structural anchor, and compact/tiered views may depend on them. Decide per-clause\nwhether compact's default takes all four or a subset, and record the reason for any clause it\ndeclines.\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO WI-fadab (related, NOT duplicate): WI-fadab is the narrower and independently\ntrue defect -- compact's three entry points disagree about whether is_excluded_kind applies\n(select_by_tokens at compact.py:1421 and format_tiered_behavior_map at :1720 call it, the default\nselect_by_coverage does not). That inconsistency is worth fixing on its own terms even if the\nshared-filter extraction lands, and a shared filter would likely subsume its user-visible effect.\nSequence WI-fadab's fix with this one rather than in parallel.\n\nWHAT THIS ROUND ESTABLISHED, carried forward from the 2026-08-01 drain: the prior 20-50% overlap\nfigure is VOID (it ranked on a stored per-node centrality field present on 0 nodes across all 8\nmaps -- verified directly), and the three candidate readings of \"centrality-ranked\" measured\n1/8 (selected set), 8/8-but-untestable-by-construction (ranked fill), and 0/8 (emitted order).\nThe owner declined to rule among those three, ruling instead on the remedy: unify the filters."  # 6bc3
- op: discuss  # 0c98
  at: '2026-08-01T23:15:07Z'  # 0c98
  by: agent  # 0c98
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0c98
  clock: 17  # 0c98
  nonce: 0c98  # 0c98
  message: "FILTER-UNIFICATION FACE CLOSED via PR #155, merged to dev 5e4fbcf7a4. Item stays OPEN and TAGGED\non the residual face -- this is an L14 advance-and-document, not a close.\n\nWHAT THE OWNER RULED (2026-08-01) AND WHAT IT RESOLVED TO: \"compact's default should filter the\nway sketch does (or use sketch's filter function(s) directly)\". There was no filter function to\ncall -- KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS was a frozenset declared INSIDE sketch._format_symbols with its four\nclauses as an inline comprehension beneath it, reachable by nothing else in the tree. So the\nruling resolved to an EXTRACTION: KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS, is_key_symbol, key_symbols and\nproduction_edges now live in selection/filters.py, whose own module header already named sketch,\ncompact and tiered JSON as its consumers. The absence of that home is why the two surfaces could\ndrift at all.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE -- measured through the PRODUCTION entry points on both sides\n(sketch._format_symbols capturing its own selected_symbols_out; compact.format_compact_behavior_map),\non the eight 07-17 maps, A/B against the same script with the source reverted:\n\n  top-10 agreement      31.2%  ->  55.0%\n  K=100 (shipped default) 42.8%  ->  73.0%\n\n8/8 repos improved or held at K=10; 8/8 improved at K=100. SwiftyJSON 16.7 -> 100, express\n18 -> 74.7, sherpa-csharp 25 -> 76.1, apollo 40 -> 62, petclinic 61.3 -> 81.8, zoxide 87.1 -> 90.6,\ncaddy 57 -> 58, pretix 37 -> 41. The 31.2% before-figure independently reproduces the 32% this\nitem recorded on 2026-08-01, which is a useful cross-check on that earlier probe.\n\nTHE COUNTER-INTUITIVE PART, and the reason to measure per clause rather than adopt wholesale: the\nEDGE filter dominates. Against sketch's ranked top-10 -- symbol filter alone 7.1/10, edge filter\nalone 8.4/10, both together 10/10 on all eight. compact had been crediting symbols for being\ncalled by their own test suites. A denylist-only variant (which would have subsumed WI-fadab)\nreached 9.4/10 and missed two repos outright, so it was rejected.\n\nRESIDUAL -- WHY THE TAG STAYS. Agreement is 55%, not 100%. With the population now shared the\nranked ORDERS match exactly; what remains is that the two surfaces apply different SELECTION\nPOLICIES over that shared ranking: compact reserves half its budget for entrypoint and\ncross-cutting seeds (the WI-vofud monotone quota), while sketch uses two-phase coverage-first\nselection with per-file caps and language-proportional allocation. That is a separate design\ndifference, not a filter divergence, and it is now the whole of what this item tracks. It is\ncohort-testable, so the tag remains correct under the worklist ruling.\n\nSCOPE HELD, recorded so a later reader does not have to re-derive it:\n  - --connectivity is EXEMPT and keeps the broader population. Its contract is bridging\n    disconnected components and a file node is frequently the only thing joining two islands;\n    narrowing it would remove the bridges the mode exists to find. Pinned by an over-reach guard\n    test that fails if someone narrows it later.\n  - Narrowing runs BEFORE seed extraction rather than at the ranking call, so it also constrains\n    force-inclusion. That is deliberate: a seed that is not a key symbol is precisely the noise\n    leading compact's output today (sherpa-csharp's top five emitted nodes were all run*.sh file\n    nodes; zoxide led with a shell completion and install.sh). This bears directly on WI-batit.\n  - `variable` is in BOTH KEY_SYMBOL_KINDS and EXCLUDED_KINDS and stays in both. A Terraform\n    variable is a real declaration surface; a CSS custom property is zero-edge noise. The two sets\n    are not complements and were never meant to be.\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO WI-fadab, corrected: this does NOT subsume it. compact's default now applies the\nALLOWLIST while its two siblings (select_by_tokens, format_tiered_behavior_map) still apply the\nis_excluded_kind DENYLIST, and the two disagree on `variable` and on any kind in neither set. The\nthree entry points are still not using one predicate -- that inconsistency is narrower now, and\nprecisely stated, but it is not gone.\n\nTESTING NOTE worth carrying: two of the three new property tests were VACUOUS on first draft and\nnow say so in place. One passed because the coverage stop had truncated the selection to a single\nsymbol, so the assertion held trivially; the other because its fixture used `calls`, a member of\nCROSS_CUTTING_EDGE_TYPES, so every endpoint became a seed candidate and the ranking under test was\nnever exercised -- the identical trap that made WI-vofud's first containment test pass for the\nwrong reason. Both carry explicit non-vacuity assertions now."  # 0c98
