  message: "DISSOLVED, not resolved. Closing done + stripping the tag. PR #157, dev fa7ae4e388.\n\nOWNER RULING (2026-08-01): compact's default flips to connectivity-aware. That takes the item's\nOWN first-listed acceptable resolution -- \"Either the spec is updated to document\nconnectivity-aware as the default and centrality-ranked as --no-connectivity, or the default is\nswitched to centrality-ranked so both surfaces agree.\" We spent July doing the second branch. The\nmeasurement says the first branch was right.\n\nWHY THE COMPLAINT DISSOLVES RATHER THAN CLOSING. The filed defect is \"sketch and compact disagree\non top symbols.\" They still do, and that is now CORRECT: they have different jobs. compact's\noutput is consumed as a GRAPH -- it emits induced-subgraph edges, and the only in-tree consumer\nof a compact map, scripts/hypergumbo_diag.py::analyze_compact, scores it on CONNECTED COMPONENTS.\nsketch is a reading surface with no graph consumer at all. An item premised on the two agreeing\nwas premised on them having the same job.\n\nTHE EVIDENCE (8 maps, 3 budgets, project's own union-find via hypergumbo_diag.connected_components):\n                       K=25            K=100           K=400\n  centrality  comps    12.6            23.6            42.1     <- worsens with budget\n              isolated 41.9%           24.2%           17.6%\n  connectivity comps    3.5             4.0             3.2     <- flat\n              isolated  8.5%            2.5%            0.3%\nAt a 25-symbol budget the centrality default was spending 42% of it on nodes with NO visible\nrelationship to anything else in the output. That is a bag of names, not a call-graph crop.\n\nWHAT THIS COST AND WHAT IT DID NOT. Flipping naively would have reverted WI-vofud's containment\nguarantee (55/120 budget pairs vs 120/120 -- see the note now on WI-vofud, whose recorded\njustification for scoping that fix narrowly turns out to be false). It did not, because the flip\nshipped WITH a containment fix for connectivity mode: seeds are interleaved 1:2 into a\nbudget-independent stream instead of preloaded, so the budget is pure truncation. Connectivity is\nnow 120/120. Fragmentation is unchanged-to-better and entrypoint reachability IMPROVES at small\nbudgets (62.0% -> 80.0% at K=25).\n\nRELATIONSHIP TO PR #155 (the sketch/compact filter unification, earlier the same day). That work\nis not wasted and is not reverted: it gave \"what counts as a key symbol\" one home in\nselection/filters.py, which sketch and the centrality path both consume. But its OBJECTIVE --\nmaking compact agree with sketch -- was the wrong objective for compact's default, and it is now\nscoped to --no-connectivity, whose stated job is precisely \"matching the sketch\". Its measured\nside effect (dropping file-kind hub nodes raised centrality-mode fragmentation, isolated\n8.2% -> 17.6% at K=400) is therefore correct for that mode rather than a regression in it, and\nevery DEFAULT consumer is strictly better off (17.6% -> 0.3%).\n\nTAG STRIPPED: the claims here were measured directly on the eight 07-17 bakeoff maps, which is\nthe cohort. There is nothing left for a future cohort to check, so under the 2026-08-01\nworklist ruling the tag does not belong.\n\nRESIDUAL, disclosed rather than closed over: format_tiered_behavior_map has the same en-bloc seed\npreload and therefore the same structural exposure, but its budget is TOKENS not symbols and its\ncontainment was never measured. Not touched here; not claimed fixed."  # ff26
